# Area Information Pano - TourMkr Design Spec

**Date:** 2026-06-23  
**Feature area:** Editor Information records and preview mode  
**Scope:** Area-linked Information modal, Information data model, preview info card, TourMkr iframe overlay

---

## Problem

Area Information can describe an indoor area with text, photos, links, and contact details, but it cannot connect that area to a 360 pano experience. Users who already have TourMkr pano URLs need a simple way to attach one pano to one Area Information record and let preview-mode viewers open the pano without leaving the floormap.

The v1 experience should be intentionally small: paste a valid TourMkr pano URL into the Information editor, show a clear pano action in preview mode, and open the pano in a full overlay modal with a single iframe.

---

## Goals

- Add a **Pano** section to the Add/Edit Information modal.
- Let each Information record store at most one TourMkr pano reference.
- Let one Area Information show at most one pano action in preview mode.
- Validate TourMkr URLs that include a tour id and pano id.
- Preserve optional heading/tilt URL parameters when present.
- Render the pano from preview mode in a full overlay modal using an iframe.
- Keep the interaction friendly and obvious without crowding the existing Area Information card.

---

## Non-Goals

- Do not support multiple panos for one Area Information record.
- Do not add a project-level TourMkr import flow.
- Do not fetch pano lists, thumbnails, or metadata from TourMkr.
- Do not add TourMkr authentication.
- Do not upload or copy pano image data into Floormap.
- Do not add pano support for Point, Door, or Safety Information in this v1.
- Do not synchronize map camera, route direction, or pano heading after the modal opens.
- Do not change the broader Information linking model.

---

## User Stories

| ID | Story | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| US-1 | As an editor user, I can paste one TourMkr pano URL into an Information record so a linked area can open a 360 pano. | P0 |
| US-2 | As an editor user, I cannot save an invalid TourMkr pano URL, so preview mode never shows a broken pano button from malformed input. | P0 |
| US-3 | As a preview viewer, I can click a pano action in an Area Information card and see the pano in a full overlay modal. | P0 |
| US-4 | As a preview viewer, I can close the pano modal and return to the same floormap preview context. | P0 |

---

## Data Model

Extend the existing `Information` interface with one optional structured pano reference:

```ts
export interface TourmkrPanoRef {
  rawUrl: string;
  tourId: string;
  panoId: string;
  heading?: number;
  tilt?: number;
}

export interface Information {
  // existing fields...
  pano?: TourmkrPanoRef;
}
```

### Rules

- `pano` is optional.
- `pano` stores one pano only.
- The original pasted URL remains in `rawUrl` and is the source of truth for the iframe source and fallback link.
- `tourId`, `panoId`, `heading`, and `tilt` are parsed at save time for validation, future compatibility, and easier testing.
- If the user clears the pano URL field, save `pano: undefined`.
- Existing Information records without `pano` continue to load normally.

### Accepted URL Format

The Pano section accepts TourMkr URLs with this shape:

```text
https://tourmkr.com/{tourId}/{panoId}p
https://tourmkr.com/{tourId}/{panoId}p&{heading}h&{tilt}t
```

Examples:

```text
https://tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p
https://tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p&29.76h&87.45t
```

Validation requirements:

- Protocol must be `https:`.
- Host must be `tourmkr.com` or `www.tourmkr.com`.
- Path must contain exactly a tour id and a pano segment.
- Pano segment must include a numeric pano id followed by `p`.
- Heading and tilt are optional.
- If heading is present, it must be parsed from `{number}h`.
- If tilt is present, it must be parsed from `{number}t`.
- Reject URLs with missing tour id, missing pano id, non-TourMkr hosts, or unsupported protocols.

---

## UX Requirements

### Information Modal

Add `Pano` as a new tab or section in `InformationModal`.

Recommended placement:

- Add a new `Pano` tab after `Media`.
- Keep the existing `Basic`, `Media`, `Contact`, `Hours`, and `Search` tabs unchanged.

Fields:

| Field | Type | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| TourMkr pano link | URL input | Stores one TourMkr pano URL only |

Recommended placeholder:

```text
https://tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p
```

Recommended helper text:

```text
Paste one TourMkr pano link for this area.
```

Validation behavior:

- Inline error if the pasted URL is invalid.
- Saving is blocked while the URL is invalid.
- Clearing the field removes the pano from the Information record.
- Editing an existing pano replaces the previous value; it does not append a second pano.

### Preview Info Card

When a selected area resolves to an Information record with a valid `pano`, show one pano action in the existing Area Information card.

Recommended action:

- A compact full-width button near the top of the card, after title/description and before other links/media.
- Label: `View 360 Pano`
- Icon: use a lucide icon such as `Orbit`, `ScanSearch`, or `Eye` if available.

Visibility:

- Show the action only for selected areas.
- Show the action only when `detail.kind === "Area"` and `detail.info?.pano` is valid.
- Do not show the action for point or safety annotations in v1, even if a reused Information record contains a pano.

### Pano Overlay Modal

Clicking `View 360 Pano` opens a full overlay modal above preview mode.

Modal requirements:

- Covers the full viewport with a dim backdrop.
- Contains a large iframe area.
- Has a clear close button in the top-right.
- Escape key closes the modal.
- Clicking outside the iframe closes the modal only if this matches the existing modal pattern; otherwise close button and Escape are enough.
- Keeps the underlying preview map mounted.
- Does not change the selected area.

Iframe requirements:

- `src` uses `pano.rawUrl`.
- `title` includes the Information title, for example `360 pano for Lobby`.
- Include `allowFullScreen`.
- Use a sandbox policy only if TourMkr still renders correctly; otherwise document why sandbox is omitted.
- Show a loading state until the iframe finishes loading.
- Show a fallback external link if the iframe fails or is blocked by TourMkr framing policy.

Recommended fallback copy:

```text
Open pano in TourMkr
```

---

## Architecture

### Parser Utility

Create a small utility for TourMkr pano parsing and formatting:

```ts
parseTourmkrPanoUrl(url: string): TourmkrPanoRef | null
isTourmkrPanoUrl(url: string): boolean
```

Recommended file:

```text
src/lib/tourmkr/pano.ts
```

The parser should use the `URL` API instead of ad hoc string splitting.

### Store And Persistence

Update the existing `Information` type in `src/store/useMapStore.ts` to include `pano?: TourmkrPanoRef`.

No new Zustand actions are required because `addInformation` and `updateInformation` already store the full Information object.

Ensure existing persistence and export paths keep the new field:

- `useWizardPersistence` should persist `informationRecords` with `pano`.
- `DigitalTwin` schema should include the extended Information type.
- Any export/import or merge path that copies Information records must preserve `pano`.

### Information Modal Save Flow

When saving:

1. Read the Pano tab URL input.
2. If empty, set `pano` to `undefined`.
3. If not empty, parse with `parseTourmkrPanoUrl`.
4. If parsing fails, show an inline error and block save.
5. If parsing succeeds, save the parsed `TourmkrPanoRef`.

### Preview Flow

1. User enters preview mode.
2. User clicks an area.
3. `PreviewOverlay` resolves `detail.info` from `AreaLayer.infoId`.
4. If the selected element is an area and the Information record has `pano`, the info card shows `View 360 Pano`.
5. Clicking the action sets local modal state, for example `activePano`.
6. `PanoOverlayModal` renders one iframe using `activePano.rawUrl`.
7. Closing the modal clears `activePano` and returns to preview mode.

---

## Files Expected To Change

| File | Action | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `src/lib/tourmkr/pano.ts` | Create | Parse and validate TourMkr pano URLs |
| `src/lib/tourmkr/__tests__/pano.test.ts` | Create | Unit tests for accepted and rejected pano URLs |
| `src/store/useMapStore.ts` | Modify | Add `TourmkrPanoRef` and `Information.pano` |
| `src/lib/digitalTwin/schema.ts` | Modify | Ensure exported Information schema preserves `pano` |
| `src/components/editor/InformationModal.tsx` | Modify | Add Pano tab/section and validation |
| `src/components/editor/PreviewOverlay.tsx` | Modify | Show pano action for area information and open modal |
| `src/components/editor/preview/PanoOverlayModal.tsx` | Create | Full overlay iframe modal |

Optional if export code uses explicit Information mapping:

| File | Action | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `src/lib/digitalTwin/mergeResults.ts` | Modify | Preserve `pano` when merging Information records |
| `src/features/wizard/steps/step4/useDigitalTwinExport.ts` | Modify | Preserve `pano` through Digital Twin export |

---

## Error Handling

- Invalid URL in the Information modal shows an inline validation error and blocks save.
- Preview mode should not render the pano action if `pano` is absent or invalid.
- If iframe loading fails or TourMkr blocks embedding, show a fallback link to open the same URL in a new tab.
- The pano modal must always be closable, including after iframe errors.
- Existing Information records should never crash if the `pano` field is missing or malformed from older saved data.

---

## Accessibility

- `View 360 Pano` is a real button with an accessible label.
- Modal uses `role="dialog"` and `aria-modal="true"`.
- Close button has an accessible label.
- Escape closes the modal.
- Focus moves into the modal when opened and returns to `View 360 Pano` when closed.
- Iframe has a descriptive `title`.

---

## Testing

### Unit Tests

Add tests for `parseTourmkrPanoUrl`:

- Parses `https://tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p`.
- Parses `https://tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p&29.76h&87.45t`.
- Accepts `https://www.tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p`.
- Rejects non-HTTPS URLs.
- Rejects non-TourMkr hosts.
- Rejects URLs without a pano id.
- Rejects malformed heading/tilt parameters.

### Component / Integration Tests

- Information modal saves a parsed pano ref when a valid TourMkr URL is entered.
- Information modal blocks save and shows an error for an invalid URL.
- Clearing the Pano field removes `pano` from the saved Information record.
- Preview info card shows `View 360 Pano` for an area linked to an Information record with `pano`.
- Preview info card does not show `View 360 Pano` for point or safety selections.
- Clicking `View 360 Pano` opens `PanoOverlayModal` with the expected iframe `src`.
- Closing the modal returns to preview mode without clearing the selected area.

### Manual QA

- Create an Information record with `https://tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p`.
- Link the Information record to one area.
- Enter preview mode, click the area, and verify `View 360 Pano` appears.
- Click `View 360 Pano` and verify the full overlay opens.
- Close the modal and verify the same area information card remains visible.
- Edit the Information record and replace the URL with `https://tourmkr.com/F1gvbw5zEr/5525144p&29.76h&87.45t`.
- Verify preview opens the updated URL.
- Try adding a second pano and verify the UI only allows replacing the existing single pano.
- Try an invalid URL and verify save is blocked.

---

## Open Questions

- Does TourMkr allow the normal share URL to render inside an iframe, or does it require a dedicated embed URL?
- Should the modal fallback external link always be visible, or only after iframe load failure?
- Should the public/published viewer outside editor preview receive the same pano button in this first implementation, or is editor preview mode enough for v1?

---

## Definition Of Done

- [ ] Information Add/Edit has a Pano section.
- [ ] One Information record can store at most one TourMkr pano reference.
- [ ] Valid TourMkr URLs with tour id and pano id can be saved.
- [ ] Valid TourMkr URLs with heading and tilt params preserve those values.
- [ ] Invalid TourMkr URLs are rejected with inline feedback.
- [ ] Area Information in preview mode shows a pano action only when a valid pano exists.
- [ ] Point and Safety Information do not show the pano action in v1.
- [ ] Clicking the pano action opens a full overlay modal.
- [ ] The modal renders the TourMkr URL in an iframe.
- [ ] The modal has a close button and Escape-to-close behavior.
- [ ] A fallback external link exists if iframe rendering fails.
- [ ] Information persistence and Digital Twin export preserve the pano field.
- [ ] Unit tests cover TourMkr URL parsing.
- [ ] Component or integration tests cover modal open/close and validation behavior.
- [ ] Lint, typecheck, and tests pass with zero new errors.
